# Workflow JSON ↔ Node codec

All conversion between user/API workflow JSON and the in-memory runtime graph **must** go through `src/codec`.

## Public API

- `jsonToNode(json)` — validate and decode a document into the runtime graph (defaults applied)
- `nodeToJson(node)` — encode a runtime graph as canonical JSON (defaults omitted, stable key order)

Do not add a second converter. `validateWorkflowDefinition` is a thin wrapper over this pair.

## Defaults

Defaults live in `WORKFLOW_DEFAULTS` (`src/codec/defaults.ts`) only.

- `jsonToNode` applies the table
- `nodeToJson` omits a field when its value is exactly a default
- Never apply these defaults outside the codec (`??`, `||`, SDK fill-ins, HTTP munging, UI helpers)

`openAsCursorGithubApp` has no factory default (the Cursor SDK chooses from the key type). Do not invent one.

## Persistence and HTTP

Store **canonical JSON** (`nodeToJson` output). GET/PATCH/list must return that shape so posting a document and reading it back cannot accumulate default fields.

Runtime (Temporal, `Agent.create` / `Agent.resume`) uses `jsonToNode` **before** the walker and SDK calls. Do not pass the stored document straight into Temporal or the SDK.

## REST / RPC / UI

REST, RPC, and any future editor **must not** reimplement JSON ↔ Node conversion or default fill/strip. Import the codec.

## CursorCloudCreateOptions

Keep the persistable agent blob slim: no `apiKey`, `local`, `mcpServers`, or subagents.
